  "physical_interpretation": "In 167Lu Table 1, the interband-to-intraband transition strength ratio B(E2)out / B(E2)in is extracted strictly from the intensity branching ratio lambda and the E2/M1 multipole mixing ratio delta. Because delta is measured via DCO / SpeeDCO without linear polarization, two mathematical roots exist: a large negative root (delta ~ -3 to -5) and a small root (delta ~ -0.07 to -0.35). The authors choose the large-delta solution based on analogy to 163Lu, which yields f_E2 = 90.6% - 96.3% and B(E2)out / B(E2)in ~ 0.23 - 0.27. If the alternative small-delta root were adopted, the extracted B(E2)out would be suppressed by a factor of 14.3 to 198.5 (reducing B(E2)out/B(E2)in to ~ 0.001 - 0.018), completely destroying the wobbling identification! Furthermore, two transitions (704.2 and 730.3 keV) lack delta values, preventing BE2 extraction. This establishes that in high-spin collective band classification, relative transition strength extraction is critically dependent on the resolution of mixing-ratio double roots."
